     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear all,</div><div><br></div><div>In climate studies, it is a common practice to perform some statistical test between two fields (maps), and then plot the resulting map using a significance mask. This masking is usually done by adding some kind of pattern (shading, crosshatching etc) on top of the actual color palette of the map.</div><div><br></div><div>Examples can be seen here in this image: <a href=\"https://www3.epa.gov/climatechange/images/science/GlobalPrecipMap-large.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www3.epa.gov/climatechange/images/science/GlobalPrecipMap-large.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367989738000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3N9unjtnNw1qq3kCL6pCxf\">https://www3.epa.gov/climatechange/images/science/GlobalPrecipMap-large.png</a> and in the left images of this panel: </div><div><a href=\"http://www.nature.com/nclimate/journal/vaop/ncurrent/images_article/nclimate2996-f3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.nature.com/nclimate/journal/vaop/ncurrent/images_article/nclimate2996-f3.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367989739000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-Qe_yyDeBvf9o6T7Xj9-W\">http://www.nature.com/nclimate/journal/vaop/ncurrent/images_article/nclimate2996-f3.jpg</a></div><div><br></div><div>In my case, I ran a statistical test for detecting trend on a time-series raster and I now have one raster with the trend for rainfall (in mm per year) and one raster with the p-values associated to the test.</div><div><br></div><div>My data looks roughly like this:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">raster</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## scratch raster objects and fill them with some random values</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trend </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raster</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrows</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncols</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xmn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">58</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xmx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">48</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">33</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">22</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trend</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">runif</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> digits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pvalue </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raster</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrows</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncols</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xmn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">58</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xmx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">48</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">33</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">22</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pvalue</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">runif</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> digits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>What I would like to do is to plot r.trend, and on top of it plot r.pvalue (as a pattern) where r.pvalues &lt; 0.01 (corresponding to a significance level of 99%).</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone here ever tried to do a similar plot using ggplot2 and can point me to any direction?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div>Thiago.</div></div>"
